{"title":"2014 IMO Problems/Problem 1","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Alternative_Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Alternative Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_IMO_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/f/4/8f4c825d5dd7e3c9485ef03ca1d225a2838ed974.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_0&lt;a_1&lt;a_2&lt;\\cdots \\quad$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"143\" height=\"12\" /> be an infinite sequence of positive integers, Prove that there exists a unique integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/0/340797a8fa9f1a06b10ce9e764998830b15ca755.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n\\ge1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"43\" height=\"14\" /> such that \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/c/4/0c463e53d0ab2ad520551056d74fad908d859cb5.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[a_n&lt;\\frac{a_0+a_1+\\cdots + a_n}{n}\\le a_{n+1}.\\]\" width=\"250\" height=\"35\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_IMO_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Define <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/3/c93db81522fd08ca9278c5879ba8f794d5ff3e65.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(n) = a_0 + a_1 + \\dots + a_n - n a_{n+1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"267\" height=\"18\" />. (In particular, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/d/0/0d08e0cd401f97d6b7223472a24001509c5db0dc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(0) = a_0.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"79\" height=\"18\" />) Notice that because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/3/b13bfa6206f20f6d8dd7f1817a84e87a9cebd735.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_{n+2} \\ge a_{n+1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"92\" height=\"16\" />, we have\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/6/c/b6c5a2a82e3e297c4f9bd804ba6094fe0cbf8303.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[a_0 + a_1 + \\dots + a_n - n a_{n+1} &gt; a_0 + a_1 + \\dots + a_n + a_{n+1} - (n+1) a_{n+2}.\\]\" width=\"478\" height=\"18\" />\nThus, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/9/ed91990ea5a798b45df5dc5b4158347cb8dd04bb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(n) &gt; f(n+1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"125\" height=\"18\" />; i.e., <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/2/bb2c93730dbb48558bb3c4738c956c4e8f816437.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"13\" height=\"18\" /> is monotonic decreasing. Therefore, because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/c/e/3ce96d94990c3599d6ad8583121ff3bc37cd9c23.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(0) &gt; 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"67\" height=\"18\" />, there exists a unique <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc97ef67268cd4e91bacdf12b8901d7036c9a056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/5/ad5edce283331d7c305b71278d5695db19923826.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(N-1) &gt; 0 \\ge f(N)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"174\" height=\"20\" />. In other words,\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/e/efe2c351c981d77210a70a5854d4990e789903fc.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[a_0 + a_1 + \\dots + a_{N-1} - (N-1) a_N &gt; 0\\]\" width=\"300\" height=\"18\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/f/6/1f6ac4d258f0999aae2bf12acf37ce7294abad82.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[a_0 + a_1 + \\dots + a_N - n a_{N+1} \\le 0.\\]\" width=\"252\" height=\"17\" />\nThis rearranges to give\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/0/7/90755de90c363f530fdf86d882df19dbbec5b47c.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[a_N &lt; \\frac{a_0 + a_1 + \\dots + a_N}{N} \\le a_{N+1}.\\]\" width=\"261\" height=\"35\" />\nDefine <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/f/0/4f0de32c7597b50a366cd5bd0181666784fcbb84.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$g(n) = a_0 + a_1 + \\dots + a_n - n a_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"250\" height=\"18\" />. Then because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/7/e/67e2dcf8777e4ef100fbc0532484f177db7d3483.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_{n+1} &gt; a_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"77\" height=\"14\" />, we have\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/7/5/f75de5ceed73b6705f562ad6191a8094291b925e.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[a_0 + a_1 + \\dots + a_n - n a_n &gt; a_0 + a_1 + \\dots + a_n + a_{n+1} - (n+1) a_{n+1}.\\]\" width=\"478\" height=\"18\" />\nTherefore, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/1/1/311cabda3a9b09f0dde217303ca9d1cd9201dcf6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$g$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> is also monotonic decreasing. Note that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/f/b/0fb7a83ac876a8cf2b6a357ea0c319a8d852c84c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$g(N+1) = a_0 + a_1 + \\dots + a_{N+1} - (N+1) a_{N+1} \\le 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"412\" height=\"18\" /> from our inequality, and so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/b/65bbdb018d6464f9121dd2d2fd05f8e62c088f83.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$g(k) \\le 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"66\" height=\"18\" /> for all <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/3/8/038008fb83bbb21fdb2aa33a19e967f9c18543c4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k &gt; N$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"51\" height=\"13\" />. Thus, the given inequality, which requires that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/f/e/5fe7b54fc88264c931a2ccd9a9389f7160900252.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$g(n) &gt; 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"67\" height=\"18\" />, cannot be satisfied for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/5/4/a54df70ab4e8f05a9ad4b78a1dad57715beaca39.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n &gt; N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"54\" height=\"15\" />, and so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc97ef67268cd4e91bacdf12b8901d7036c9a056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> is the unique solution to this inequality.\n</p><p>--<a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=User:Suli&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"User:Suli (page does not exist)\">Suli</a> 22:38, 7 February 2015 (EST)\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Alternative_Solution\">Alternative Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_IMO_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Alternative Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>It is more convenient to work with differences <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/d/d/1dd08422f0b39f5160e1874d0107aa31138d1fdb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d_i=a_i-a_{i-1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"111\" height=\"18\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/d/7/dd7f929cd158aba676412be97fb5fa4fdca3d635.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$i\\ge 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"41\" height=\"16\" />. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/9/f/89f57945941aef0976c94fa138f8edd209939511.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d_i\\ge 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"50\" height=\"17\" />. Instead of using <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/8/e/f8e93bd75e710a291a9280912244d0c687512527.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_i=a_0+d_1+\\ldots+d_i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"178\" height=\"17\" /> the inequalities can be rewritten in terms of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/1/5/f1544d77330dc5a289ad6a42beeb236b8dd70a9a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d_i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"14\" height=\"15\" /> as \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/8/ef8c356e450bfcaebbb2b520ca60230be57e4781.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[0 &lt; V_n \\le nd_{n+1}\\]\" width=\"121\" height=\"17\" /> \nwhere <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/f/6af88a46419ada12b8ab9788862435d4765521bd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$V_n=a_0-d_2-2d_3-3d_4-\\ldots - (n-1)d_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"339\" height=\"20\" />. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/4/4/744280a1131dbc09035f25e742e47d526d6e64fe.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$V_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"18\" height=\"15\" /> is strictly monotonically decreasing. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/6/3/b63fb54d4e40dd7e7c3e811d3019695c1f5bf82e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$V_1=a_0 &gt;0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"95\" height=\"17\" />. That is the left inequality is satisfied for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/d/9/1d96ecc15129c5631ba4a2c6578e91e3d13e3baf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"46\" height=\"14\" />. Lets take a look at the time step <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/9/c/99cb3f3a8b3bbfc702c5863d16602a06cded535d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(n+1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"54\" height=\"18\" /> which is right after <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />:  <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/2/e/92ed6c61fe62ac0313ce59f7d8e8bc0aef5222b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n \\rightarrow n+1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"83\" height=\"15\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/d/f3d7449a2426b8bd935ec527eb689f529bd017ca.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[0&lt; V_n-nd_{n+1}\\le  (n+1)d_{n+2}\\]\" width=\"234\" height=\"18\" /> \nThe condition <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/c/4/ec4dc314dc9b64ab3fbc9dc07cfb583bd578e514.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$V_n \\le nd_{n+1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"92\" height=\"18\" />for breaking the left inequality at some step <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/e/3/0e3efd9b14723a92c2ae891fe27780d5f8e2b215.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n+1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"44\" height=\"15\" /> is exactly the condition for satisfying the right inequality at step <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />. Once left inequality is broken at step <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/9/c/99cb3f3a8b3bbfc702c5863d16602a06cded535d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(n+1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"54\" height=\"18\" /> it will remain broken for future steps as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/4/4/744280a1131dbc09035f25e742e47d526d6e64fe.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$V_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"18\" height=\"15\" /> is strictly decreasing. The right inequality will be satisfied for some <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/4/4/744280a1131dbc09035f25e742e47d526d6e64fe.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$V_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"18\" height=\"15\" /> is strictly decreasing integer sequence and the right hand side <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/8/2/382d530a75b9f0fc86356ec070cc81ac60f10852.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$nd_{n+1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"48\" height=\"18\" /> of the right inequality is bounded by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> from below. In summary, the left inequality is satisfied initially and as soon as the right inequality is satisfied, which will happen for some <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />, the left inequality will break at the very next step and will remain broken for all future steps. That is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> when both inequalities are satisfied exists and unique.\n</p><p>--<a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=User:Alexander_skabelin&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"User:Alexander skabelin (page does not exist)\">alexander_skabelin</a> 9:24, 7 July 2023 (EST)\n</p><p><i>Alternate solutions are always welcome. If you have a different, elegant solution to this problem, please <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=2014_IMO_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit\">add it</a> to this page.</i>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_IMO_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"clear:both; margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_IMO\" title=\"2014 IMO\">2014 IMO</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_IMO_Problems\" title=\"2014 IMO Problems\">Problems</a></b>) • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/community/c3222\">Resources</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"33%\" align=\"center\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b>First Problem</b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"34%\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_IMO_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2014 IMO Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_IMO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2014 IMO Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_IMO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2014 IMO Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_IMO_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2014 IMO Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_IMO_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2014 IMO Problems/Problem 6\">6</a>\n</td>\n<td width=\"33%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_IMO_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2014 IMO Problems/Problem 2\">Problem 2</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=IMO_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"IMO Problems and Solutions\"> All IMO Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_IMO_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017182613\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.035 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.053 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 300/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 1210/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 51/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 4/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 9274/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   12.833      1 -total\n 57.22%    7.343      1 Template:IMO_box\n 41.74%    5.357      1 Template:Alternate_solutions\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:13388:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017182613 and revision id 195418. Rendering was triggered because: page-view\n -->\n</div>"}